{%- comment -%}
Homelab status for the TRMNL terminal. One polling URL:

  https://terminal.lsck0.dev/<token>/stats.json

Everything is precomputed by src/scripts/stats-sync.py: Liquid cannot do
arithmetic worth relying on, so percentages, human-readable rates and the bar
widths all arrive ready to render.

Monochrome e-ink, 800x480. No colour to spend, so state is carried by shape:
a filled square is up and a hollow one is down. VMs switched off on purpose
are named in one grey line at the foot of the grid rather than given a row
each - eighteen rows reading 0/0 for ever is where the free space went.

Kept flat, one tag per line. Do not run "Fix indentation" on it.
{%- endcomment -%}

<style>
/* TRMNL's .layout centres and pads a single child, which renders a full-bleed
   dashboard as a narrow column in the middle of the screen. */
.layout { display: block !important; width: 100% !important; height: 100% !important; padding: 0 !important; margin: 0 !important; }
/* Fill the box we are given, not the viewport. 100vh was wrong because the
   markup editor previews in a container far taller than it is tall: the rows
   stretched past the visible area and only three of the month's six weeks
   fitted. 100% tracks whatever TRMNL hands us, and min-height keeps the
   layout from collapsing if that parent turns out to have no definite
   height, which is what made an earlier version render blank. max-height
   keeps the content clear of the title bar, which is drawn over the page. */
.hl { display: flex; flex-direction: column; height: 100%; min-height: 422px; max-height: calc(100vh - 58px); width: 100%; gap: 5px; padding: 8px 10px 4px; box-sizing: border-box; }

/* ---- headline numbers ------------------------------------------------- */
.hl-top { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex: 0 0 auto; }
.hl-stat { flex: 1 1 0; border: 2px solid #000; padding: 2px 7px; min-width: 0; }
.hl-stat--bad { background: #000; }
.hl-stat--bad .hl-k, .hl-stat--bad .hl-v { color: #fff; }
.hl-k { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .10em; text-transform: uppercase; }
.hl-v { font-size: 25px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.05; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
/* two rates in one tile, so they have to give up some size */
.hl-v--pair { font-size: 15px; white-space: nowrap; }
.hl-sub { font-size: 12px; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }

/* ---- services --------------------------------------------------------- */
.hl-mid { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 0; }
.hl-left { flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; min-height: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 5px; }
.hl-svc { flex: 0 0 auto; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-content: flex-start; gap: 0 10px; min-width: 0; min-height: 0; border: 2px solid #000; padding: 3px 6px; overflow: hidden; }
/* Four columns of eight: only the VMs that are meant to be running. The
   eighteen switched off on purpose spent a third of the panel saying 0/0 for
   ever, so they are one line of names at the foot instead, which is what
   bought the clients band its height. A quarter column is 128px, so the
   numeric percentages had to go; the two bars carry the same reading. */
.hl-row { width: calc(25% - 8px); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.32; min-width: 0; }
.hl-dot { width: 8px; height: 8px; flex: 0 0 auto; border: 1px solid #000; background: #000; }
.hl-dot--off { background: #fff; }
.hl-name { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
/* the two bars share one track so a busy VM reads at a glance without numbers */
.hl-bars { flex: 0 0 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }
.hl-bar { height: 4px; background: #d2d2d2; }
.hl-bar span { display: block; height: 100%; background: #000; }
.hl-off { width: 100%; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.25; color: #555; border-top: 1px solid #d2d2d2; margin-top: 2px; padding-top: 2px; }
.hl-off b { font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #000; }

/* ---- who is calling ---------------------------------------------------- */
/* The Prometheus metrics know nothing about clients, so this band comes from
   Traefik's access log by way of Loki: the country Cloudflare stamped on the
   request, the browser family, the hostname asked for, and how the lot went.
   Each row carries a bar of its share of the biggest row in its column - a
   share of the total would make everything under the leader a sliver.
   The grid above takes its natural height and this takes what is left, so
   the band is the one that has to be cut to fit: eight rows of 16px in the
   133px left over once the header has its 16. */
.hl-who { flex: 1 1 auto; border: 2px solid #000; padding: 3px 7px; display: flex; gap: 12px; min-height: 0; overflow: hidden; }
.hl-who-col { flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
.hl-who-h { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; border-bottom: 1px solid #000; margin-bottom: 1px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 6px; white-space: nowrap; flex: 0 0 auto; }
.hl-who-h i { font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; color: #555; }
.hl-who-l { position: relative; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 6px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.34; flex: 0 0 auto; }
.hl-who-l i { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 1px; bottom: 1px; background: #e0e0e0; }
.hl-who-l span, .hl-who-l b { position: relative; }
.hl-who-l span { overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; min-width: 0; padding-left: 2px; }
.hl-who-l b { flex: 0 0 auto; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; padding-right: 2px; }

/* ---- side panels ------------------------------------------------------ */
.hl-side { flex: 0 0 216px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 5px; min-height: 0; }
/* 0 0 auto, not the flex default: a shrinkable panel silently gives up the
   bottom half of its last row when the column is tight, which is how the
   requests list came to show three and a half entries. The lists are cut to
   size in stats-sync instead, and only the torrents panel takes up slack. */
.hl-panel { flex: 0 0 auto; border: 2px solid #000; padding: 3px 7px; min-height: 0; min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
.hl-panel--grow { flex: 1 1 auto; }
.hl-h { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .10em; text-transform: uppercase; border-bottom: 1px solid #000; margin-bottom: 2px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }
.hl-line { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 6px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.3; }
.hl-line b { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.hl-req { overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; min-width: 0; }
/* int = arrived over the LAN or the mesh, ext = relayed in off the
   internet, + = both. Traefik carries no client address, so this is as
   precise as "from where" gets. */
.hl-req i { font-style: normal; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #555; }
.hl-t { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.25; margin-top: 2px; min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; }
/* a release name is longer than the panel and a magnet-only torrent is a
   40-character hash, so one clamped line either way */
.hl-t-name { display: block; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; font-weight: 700; max-width: 100%; }
.hl-t-meta { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 11px; }
.hl-prog { height: 4px; background: #d2d2d2; margin-top: 1px; }
.hl-prog span { display: block; height: 100%; background: #000; }
.hl-empty { font-size: 12px; }
</style>

{% if view == 'stats' %}
<div class="layout">
<div class="hl">

<div class="hl-top">
<div class="hl-stat{% if summary.down.size > 0 %} hl-stat--bad{% endif %}">
<div class="hl-k">Services &middot; cpu/mem</div>
<div class="hl-v">{{ summary.up }}/{{ summary.total }}</div>
</div>
<div class="hl-stat">
<div class="hl-k">CPU &middot; {{ totals.cores }} cores</div>
<div class="hl-v">{{ totals.cpu_pct }}%</div>
</div>
<div class="hl-stat">
<div class="hl-k">Memory &middot; {{ totals.mem_total }}</div>
<div class="hl-v">{{ totals.mem_pct }}%</div>
</div>
<div class="hl-stat">
<div class="hl-k">Network</div>
<div class="hl-v hl-v--pair">&darr;{{ network.rx }} &uarr;{{ network.tx }}</div>
</div>
<div class="hl-stat">
<div class="hl-k">Torrents</div>
<div class="hl-v">{{ torrents.downloading }}/{{ torrents.total }}</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="hl-mid">

<div class="hl-left">

<div class="hl-svc">
{% for s in services %}
<div class="hl-row">
<span class="hl-dot{% unless s.online %} hl-dot--off{% endunless %}"></span>
<span class="hl-name">{{ s.name }}</span>
<span class="hl-bars"><span class="hl-bar"><span style="width:{{ s.cpu_pct }}%"></span></span><span class="hl-bar"><span style="width:{{ s.mem_pct }}%"></span></span></span>
</div>
{% endfor %}
{% if services_off.size > 0 %}
<div class="hl-off"><b>Off &middot; {{ services_off.size }}</b> &nbsp;{{ services_off | join: " &middot; " }}</div>
{% endif %}
</div>

<div class="hl-who">
{% if clients.available %}
<div class="hl-who-col">
<div class="hl-who-h"><span>From</span><i>{{ clients.window }}</i></div>
{% for c in clients.countries %}
<div class="hl-who-l"><i style="width:{{ c.pct }}%"></i><span>{{ c.name }}</span><b>{{ c.count }}</b></div>
{% endfor %}
</div>
<div class="hl-who-col">
<div class="hl-who-h"><span>Clients</span></div>
{% for a in clients.agents %}
<div class="hl-who-l"><i style="width:{{ a.pct }}%"></i><span>{{ a.name }}</span><b>{{ a.count }}</b></div>
{% endfor %}
</div>
<div class="hl-who-col">
<div class="hl-who-h"><span>Asking for</span></div>
{% for h in clients.hosts %}
<div class="hl-who-l"><i style="width:{{ h.pct }}%"></i><span>{{ h.name }}</span><b>{{ h.count }}</b></div>
{% endfor %}
</div>
<div class="hl-who-col">
<div class="hl-who-h"><span>How it went</span></div>
{% for t in clients.traffic %}
<div class="hl-who-l"><i style="width:{{ t.pct }}%"></i><span>{{ t.name }}</span><b>{{ t.count }}</b></div>
{% endfor %}
</div>
{% else %}
<div class="hl-who-col"><div class="hl-who-h"><span>Who is calling</span></div><div class="hl-who-l"><span>no access log in Loki</span></div></div>
{% endif %}
</div>

</div>

<div class="hl-side">

<div class="hl-panel">
<div class="hl-h"><span>Requests</span><span>/min</span></div>
{% for r in requests %}
<div class="hl-line"><span class="hl-req">{{ r.name }} <i>{{ r.origin }}{% if r.mixed %}+{% endif %}</i></span><b>{{ r.rpm }}</b></div>
{% endfor %}
{% if requests.size == 0 %}<div class="hl-empty">no traffic</div>{% endif %}
</div>

<div class="hl-panel">
<div class="hl-h"><span>Disks</span><span>{{ storage.free_total }} free</span></div>
{% for d in storage.top %}
<div class="hl-line"><span>{{ d.vm }}{% unless d.mount == '/' %} {{ d.mount }}{% endunless %}</span><b>{{ d.pct }}%</b></div>
{% endfor %}
</div>

<div class="hl-panel hl-panel--grow">
<div class="hl-h"><span>Torrents</span><span>&darr;{{ torrents.dl }} &uarr;{{ torrents.ul }}</span></div>
{% if torrents.available %}
<div class="hl-line"><span>down / seed / paused</span><b>{{ torrents.downloading }} / {{ torrents.seeding }} / {{ torrents.paused }}</b></div>
{% for t in torrents.items %}
<div class="hl-t">
<div class="hl-t-name">{{ t.name }}</div>
<div class="hl-prog"><span style="width:{{ t.pct }}%"></span></div>
<div class="hl-t-meta"><span>{{ t.pct }}% &middot; {{ t.size }}</span><span>{{ t.speed }}{% if t.eta != '' %} &middot; {{ t.eta }}{% endif %}</span></div>
</div>
{% endfor %}
{% if torrents.total == 0 %}<div class="hl-empty">nothing queued</div>{% endif %}
{% else %}
<div class="hl-empty">qBittorrent unreachable</div>
{% endif %}
</div>

</div>
</div>

</div>
</div>
<div class="title_bar">
<span class="title">Homelab</span>
<span class="instance">{{ label }}{% if summary.down.size > 0 %} &middot; down: {{ summary.down | join: ", " }}{% endif %}{% if services_more > 0 %} &middot; +{{ services_more }} more{% endif %}</span>
</div>

{% else %}
<div class="layout">
<div class="markdown">
<span class="title">Homelab: no data</span>
<div class="content">No `view` in the payload. Check the plugin's Polling URL points at stats.json on terminal.lsck0.dev.</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="title_bar"><span class="title">Homelab</span><span class="instance">waiting for data</span></div>
{% endif %}
